      <h2 class="section-heading blue">Merchant Initiated Transactions (MIT)</h2>
      <p style="color:#666; font-size:0.9em; margin-top:-0.25rem; margin-bottom:1rem;">
        Off-session charges against previously vaulted payment methods using stored-credential fields
        (<code>payment_initiator: MERCHANT</code>, <code>usage: SUBSEQUENT</code>). Requires prior customer consent at vault time.
      </p>
      <section class="integrations-gallery">

        <a href="/mit/v5" class="integration-card">
          <span class="sdk-badge js-sdk-v5">★ JS SDK v5</span>
          <span class="sdk-badge server-sdk">✓ Server SDK</span>
<h3>MIT — JS SDK v5</h3>
          <p><strong>Off-Session Charge (v5 Vault)</strong></p>
          <p>Charge a payment token vaulted via the JS SDK v5 without the customer present.</p>
          <ul>
            <li>Lookup vaulted token by Customer ID</li>
            <li>Stored-credential fields on order</li>
            <li>Authorize or capture immediately</li>
            <li>No buyer redirect needed</li>
          </ul>
        </a>

        <a href="/mit/v6" class="integration-card">
          <span class="sdk-badge js-sdk-v6">⬡ JS SDK v6</span>
          <span class="sdk-badge server-sdk">✓ Server SDK</span>
<h3>MIT — JS SDK v6</h3>
          <p><strong>Off-Session Charge (v6 Vault)</strong></p>
          <p>Charge a token vaulted during a v6 SDK session. Vault setup via web components; MIT charge is server-side.</p>
          <ul>
            <li>v6 SDK handles customer-present vault</li>
            <li>Stored-credential fields on MIT order</li>
            <li>Authorize or capture immediately</li>
            <li>No buyer redirect needed</li>
          </ul>
        </a>

        <a href="/mit/api" class="integration-card">
          <span class="sdk-badge rest-api">⚠ Direct REST API</span>
          <span class="sdk-badge server-sdk">✓ Server SDK</span>
<h3>MIT — Direct REST API</h3>
          <p><strong>Fully Server-Side MIT</strong></p>
          <p>Vault and MIT charge both via REST — no JS SDK at any stage. Full control over stored-credential payload.</p>
          <ul>
            <li>Server-side vault setup &amp; token exchange</li>
            <li>Full <code>stored_credential</code> block control</li>
            <li>Network transaction ID passthrough</li>
            <li>Authorize or capture immediately</li>
          </ul>
        </a>

      </section>


